# Necromancy is sacrificed at cleanup only if it was cast at a time a sorcery couldn't have been by its own "as though it had
# flash" permission (its 2022-12-08 ruling: cast by some other effect, it isn't). Bot1's Bloodbraid Challenger cascades into
# it (CR 702.85a), and Bot1 casts it as the cascade trigger resolves, with the Challenger still on the stack: by cascade's
# permission, not its own. With no creature card in any graveyard it stays a plain enchantment, and nothing sacrifices it at
# the cleanup step: no delayed triggered ability was created (CR 608.3g).

